cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this repository and the paper it
  accompanies. The code is licensed under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later.
title: >-
  One ECG lead carries far more than atrial fibrillation (code)
abstract: >-
  Code, aggregated results and figures for a study of ECG encoders trained without
  any diagnosis on open hospital recordings (MIMIC-IV-ECG) and read out frozen with
  one logistic regression per finding. An autoencoder on the averaged heartbeat,
  reproduced from Friedman et al. (2025), is compared with a masked autoencoder on
  the whole ten-second strip, on a handheld single-lead device, on an external
  twelve-lead cohort reduced to one, two and twelve leads, and on hospital diagnoses
  of MIMIC-IV patients not seen in training. No ECG data, patient
  records, trained weights or manuscript are included.
type: software
